{"ts":"2026-11-13T17:15:36.033Z","type":"escaped","story":"BUG-10","decisionId":"472c3014-3c68-483f-961f-a6260e85dff7","subtaskId":"self","source":"arch-review","findings":[{"severity":"blocking","category":"correctness","file":"src/Ordering.API/Application/Commands/IdentifiedCommandHandler.cs","issue":"The catch/rethrow of OrderingDomainException applies to every IdentifiedCommandHandler subclass. CreateOrderAsync (OrdersApi.cs:201) has no try/catch, so a rule or validation failure on create order now becomes an unhandled exception instead of the previous handled outcome. SetPaid, SetStockConfirme"},{"severity":"blocking","category":"correctness","file":"src/Ordering.API/Application/Commands/IdentifiedCommandHandler.cs","issue":"CreateRequestForCommandAsync persists the request id before the command runs. After a rejected cancel or ship (409/400) the id stays stored, and a retry with the same x-requestid returns 200 through the duplicate-request path, a false success for an operation that failed."}],"files":[],"delivery":"epic"}
{"ts":"2026-11-13T17:38:00.442Z","type":"story","story":"BUG-10","decisionId":"472c3014-3c68-483f-961f-a6260e85dff7","mode":"self","outcome":"done","reason":null,"tokens":4104100,"cost":2.934482,"premiumRequests":null,"wallClockSec":1828,"agentRuns":4,"reviewBlocks":1,"bugFixCycles":0,"limitHit":null,"branch":"feat/bug-10-be-ordering-api-invalid-order-status-changes-return-5","lspCalls":7,"signatureChangesWithoutReferences":false,"followUps":[{"title":"Cancel/ship endpoints do not check order ownership or role","reason":"Any authenticated user can cancel or ship any order number; ship should be admin-only.","subtask":"self","round":1},{"title":"Request id for a not-found cancel/ship is recorded before the 404","reason":"A retry with the same request id returns 200 although nothing happened.","subtask":"self","round":1}],"delivery":"epic"}
